findings.body:
**The structural check covers fewer paths than the list it replaces.** The test only checks files whose name starts with one of the 7 listed concepts. Checked against `src/core/{types,constants,errors,enums}`:

- **Empty concepts:** `store` and `hooks` match no file. The store's extracted files are named after their repositories (`session.types.ts`, `ledger.types.ts`, ...), and `profile-store.errors.ts` does not start with `store`. With `extracted` empty, `standard` is `[]`, so both tests pass without checking anything.
- **Paths that lost their check:** the old `it.each` pinned these and no test checks them now: `enums/merge-status.enums.ts`, `enums/gate-stage-status.enums.ts`, `types/land.types.ts`, `types/regate.types.ts`, `enums/interrupt-signal.enums.ts`, `types/session.types.ts`, `enums/session-state.enums.ts`, `errors/session.errors.ts`, `types/ledger.types.ts`, `types/baseline-history.types.ts`, `types/decision-record.types.ts`, `errors/git-diff.errors.ts`, `types/git-diff.types.ts`, `types/github.types.ts`.

**Mutant:** delete `'src/core/types/land*'` from [CRITICAL_AREAS](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/65b3d783989d985f2b8fb9f44c385478fedace6c/src/core/routing.utils.ts#L21-L57). In a glob, `*` never crosses a `/` (`glob.utils.ts:21`), so `src/core/land*` does not cover `types/land.types.ts`. After the deletion, `tierForScope(['src/core/types/land.types.ts'])` returns `Standard` and no test fails. The same goes for a new extraction such as `src/core/enums/git-ref.enums.ts`: `git` is not a concept. So the PR's acceptance criterion holds only for the concepts listed, and two of those check nothing.

**Fix:** use prefixes that match how the critical files are really named, and fail when a concept matches nothing ([L78-L101](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/65b3d783989d985f2b8fb9f44c385478fedace6c/src/core/routing-utils.test.ts#L78-L101)). On today's tree each of these prefixes matches at least one file, and every matched file routes critical. The `.` in `'session.'` keeps out `session-cap` and `session-handoff`. Keep `'session-lifecycle'` in the list only if you keep its new CRITICAL_AREAS globs (see the finding on `routing.utils.ts:45`).

```ts
describe.each([
  'sandbox', 'merge-gate', 'merge-status', 'gate-stage-status', 'land', 'regate',
  'interrupt-signal', 'profile-compiler', 'git', 'session.', 'session-state',
  'event-type', 'ledger', 'baseline-history', 'decision-record',
])('the %s concept', (concept) => {
  // ...extracted as before...
  it('routes every extracted file critical', () => {
    expect(extracted).not.toEqual([]);
    // ...standard check as before...
  });
});
```
